 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Provides that the thruway authority shall issue permits for ambulances and fire vehicles exempting such vehicles from paying tolls on the thruway when engaged in an emergency operation.",
 "title": "Provides that the thruway authority shall issue permits for ambulances and fire vehicles for toll exemptions",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A34",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A34-2025",
     "printNo": "A34",
     "session": 2025,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 55\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 34, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  public authorities law, in relation to the\n      issuance of permits to exempt ambulances and  fire  vehicles  from\n      paying  tolls  on  the  New  York state thruway when engaged in an\n      emergency operation\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would duplicate the existing process for  emergency  service\ntoll  reimbursement  for  ambulance  and fire vehicles traveling the New\nYork State Thruway.\n \n  Consistent with Public Authorities  Law  Section  378-a,  the  Thruway\nAuthority  already  provides  emergency  service  toll reimbursement for\nambulance and fire vehicles that travel on the  Thruway.  In  2023,  the\nThruway  Authority  implemented  streamlined  emergency  responder  toll\nreimbursement procedures. Though  this  bill  is  well-intentioned,  the\nproposed requirement to issue permits for no-charge travel creates audit\ndifficulties  and may encourage use outside the scope of eligible travel\nand in other vehicles.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 55,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2025
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
